 "relevance_note": "Review of LCAT deficiency with one first-hand case: 'Genetic analysis identified two mutations, heterozygous on the LCAT gene'.",
 "method_note": "Read the paper by hand; no table transcribed by script. In scope: the case-report patient ('patient', rule 5) and one previously published person mentioned in passing ('These two mutations have been previously described in one other patient (with similar findings: very low HDL and no cardiovascular disease)'), labelled 'unnamed person 1' because no reference is printed for that person; included under v4 because the paper gives that person's variants and features. Group-level cohorts in the review (Hovingh, Calabresi, Canadian study with two homozygotes and seven heterozygotes) give no individual-level detail and get no rows. Zygosity 'heterozygous' recorded per the paper's wording 'two mutations, heterozygous on the LCAT gene'; the paper does not say compound heterozygous or in trans, so not recorded as such. Variant type not recorded (Tyr83Stp is not called nonsense in the text). Table 1 gives ApoA1 0.39 g/L, triglycerides 2.55 mmol/L and LDL 2.27 mmol/L without calling them low or high and without reference ranges, so the matching checklist items are 'not reported'. 'normal clinical examination' and 'no significant ... past medical history' exclude nothing specific and were not recorded. Possible inconsistency: 'no significant familial ... history' vs 'It was not possible to complete a family history of this patient, as she did not know her family'; no parental testing reported. Age 52 recorded as age at last evaluation (presentation); no separate age at diagnosis stated. cites_prior_report_of_same_patients left null: the paper says the mutations, not this patient, were previously described.",
